The run is ending without a verified fix. Reason: {{ reason }}.

Write a handoff for the human who picks this up. They have not seen any of the
above and are starting cold.

Reply with a single JSON object and nothing else — no prose before or after, no
code fences. Use exactly this shape:

{
  "root_cause_hypotheses": [
    {
      "statement": "what you believe is wrong, specifically",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "evidence": ["the observations supporting it, quoted concretely"]
    }
  ],
  "what_was_ruled_out": ["hypotheses eliminated, each with what eliminated it"],
  "suggested_next_steps": ["what to do next, in order, most useful first"],
  "blocking_reason": null
}

Order hypotheses most likely first, and let `confidence` reflect the evidence
rather than optimism — a well-calibrated 0.4 is more useful than a reflexive
0.9. If you have no real hypothesis, say so in one entry with low confidence
rather than inventing one.

Set `blocking_reason` to a short machine-readable string when one specific thing
stopped you, otherwise null. Use `fix_not_expressible_in_values` when the fix
requires editing a chart template rather than a values file, and name that
template path in `suggested_next_steps`.
